Remove Duplicates from Sorted List (LeetCode 83)

Optimal Solution

Approach:
Since the linked list is sorted, all duplicate values will be next to each other.
Traverse the list using a pointer temp.
For every node:
Store the next node in nextNode.
Check if nextNode has the same value as temp.
If duplicates are found, keep moving nextNode until a different value is found.
Connect temp->next with the next unique node.
Move temp forward and repeat.

Idea: Keep the first occurrence of every value and remove all repeated occurrences after it.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Every node is visited once while traversing.

Space Complexity: O(1)
No extra data structure is used.

Code : 

/**
 * Definition for singly-linked list.
 * struct ListNode {
 *     int val;
 *     ListNode *next;
 *     ListNode() : val(0), next(nullptr) {}
 *     ListNode(int x) : val(x), next(nullptr) {}
 *     ListNode(int x, ListNode *next) : val(x), next(next) {}
 * };
 */

class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* deleteDuplicates(ListNode* head) {

        ListNode* temp = head;

        while (temp != nullptr && temp->next != nullptr) {

            // Start checking from next node
            ListNode* nextNode = temp->next;

            // Skip all duplicate nodes
            while (nextNode != nullptr && nextNode->val == temp->val) {

                ListNode* dupl = nextNode;
                nextNode = nextNode->next;

                delete dupl;
            }

            // Connect current node with next unique node
            temp->next = nextNode;

            // Move to next unique node
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        return head;
    }
};
